{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00539",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.8,
      "end_seconds": 6.61,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Morning. Just so I've got the right file, are you Maya Kowalczyk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.8,
      "end_seconds": 9.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "That's me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.13,
      "end_seconds": 16.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "I'll do my best. And you've brought a notebook, I see. Very organised."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.64,
      "end_seconds": 30.79,
      "duration_seconds": 12.15,
      "text": "I keep a diary. Since the cast came off I've written down how the wrist feels every day, otherwise I forget the details once I'm here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.93,
      "end_seconds": 39.02,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Brilliant, I love a diary. Where would you like to start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.32,
      "end_seconds": 51.47,
      "duration_seconds": 10.15,
      "text": "The stiffness in my wrist. I can't turn my hand over properly. The cast came off two weeks ago and it's hardly improved."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.83,
      "end_seconds": 59.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "Which wrist is it, and when is it at its worst?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.64,
      "end_seconds": 66.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.8,
      "text": "Right wrist. Mornings, according to the diary. It eases by lunchtime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.33,
      "end_seconds": 70.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "And is there pain with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.68,
      "end_seconds": 83.77,
      "duration_seconds": 11.09,
      "text": "Pain when I rotate my hand, like turning a door handle or opening a jar. A sharp twinge on the thumb side. I'd say moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.46,
      "end_seconds": 89.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Jars are the classic. Does anything ease it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.35,
      "end_seconds": 100.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Warm water. I stand at the sink with my hand under the tap."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.46,
      "end_seconds": 105.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Anything else you've noticed about the hand itself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.85,
      "end_seconds": 118.71,
      "duration_seconds": 10.86,
      "text": "It swells a bit by evening, the back of the wrist looks puffy. And my grip is weak. I dropped my favourite mug on Sunday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.62,
      "end_seconds": 124.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Oh no, not the favourite. What was it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.13,
      "end_seconds": 130.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "One my sister made. I've glued it back together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.04,
      "end_seconds": 137.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Ha, very kintsugi. Right, a few more questions. Any numbness in your fingers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.89,
      "end_seconds": 142.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "No, none of that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.15,
      "end_seconds": 147.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Does the wrist wake you at night?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.35,
      "end_seconds": 155.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.6,
      "text": "No, I sleep fine. It only bothers me when I use it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.91,
      "end_seconds": 159.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Any fever lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.83,
      "end_seconds": 164.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.54,
      "end_seconds": 168.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "And any redness over the wrist?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.63,
      "end_seconds": 174.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "No, it looks normal apart from the puffiness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.74,
      "end_seconds": 181.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.24,
      "text": "Thanks. Now tell me about your general health. Anything long-term?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.74,
      "end_seconds": 190.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "Reflux, on and off for years. And osteopenia, they found it a couple of years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.49,
      "end_seconds": 199.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.55,
      "text": "Good thinking, the osteopenia matters here. Any bone problems in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.91,
      "end_seconds": 206.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "My mother had osteoporosis. She broke her hip at seventy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.78,
      "end_seconds": 212.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "I'm sorry to hear that. Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.77,
      "end_seconds": 218.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Only my appendix out, when I was fifteen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.77,
      "end_seconds": 224.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies, to medicines or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.46,
      "end_seconds": 230.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.94,
      "end_seconds": 235.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "What do you do for work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.87,
      "end_seconds": 245.66,
      "duration_seconds": 7.79,
      "text": "I'm an illustrator, so it's all tablet and pen, which is why this is such a disaster."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.51,
      "end_seconds": 252.64,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "And do you have a drink, at the end of the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.8,
      "end_seconds": 261.01,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "A glass of wine on weekends, no more than that. And I've never smoked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.94,
      "end_seconds": 266.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Good. Are you taking anything for the pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.94,
      "end_seconds": 277.24,
      "duration_seconds": 10.3,
      "text": "Ibuprofen, from the chemist. Maybe 200 milligrams? I just take the little pills, a couple a day. I'm not sure of the strength."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.76,
      "end_seconds": 285.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "Okay, we'll come back to that. Any chest pain or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.75,
      "end_seconds": 290.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.32,
      "end_seconds": 296.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "And any shortness of breath or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.78,
      "end_seconds": 299.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "No, my breathing's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.39,
      "end_seconds": 306.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Let me take your numbers while we're here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.12,
      "end_seconds": 327.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.16,
      "text": "Blood pressure is 124 over 78, pulse is 72, temperature is 36.7 degrees, and oxygen is 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.1,
      "end_seconds": 336.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "You're 63 kilograms on the scales as well. Now hold both hands out, palms down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.7,
      "end_seconds": 358.43,
      "duration_seconds": 11.73,
      "text": "Mild swelling over the back of the wrist on the right, yes. Now bend the wrist back as far as you can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.44,
      "end_seconds": 364.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "That's as far as it goes. It pulls right here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.26,
      "end_seconds": 380.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "It only goes about half as far as the other side. Now close your eyes and tell me which fingertip I touch."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 383.05,
      "end_seconds": 387.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Index... middle... little finger. Ring finger. Thumb."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.2,
      "end_seconds": 394.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "All correct, so the feeling in all your fingertips is normal, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.43,
      "end_seconds": 400.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "So what's going on? Is the bone not mended?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.39,
      "end_seconds": 417.08,
      "duration_seconds": 14.69,
      "text": "From what I see, this looks like stiffness after being in a cast, which is very common. But I can't rule out that the small bone isn't fully healed yet, so I'd like to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.64,
      "end_seconds": 420.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Check how?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 422.43,
      "end_seconds": 434.42,
      "duration_seconds": 11.99,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an X-ray of the wrist, today if we can. And I'd also order a blood test for your vitamin D, given the osteopenia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 435.27,
      "end_seconds": 438.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "And if the vitamin D is low?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 439.54,
      "end_seconds": 447.27,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "Then I might consider a bone density scan, but we'll hold off on that for now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 449.6,
      "end_seconds": 455.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "Okay. And the pain? The ibuprofen hasn't been doing much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 456.21,
      "end_seconds": 468.88,
      "duration_seconds": 12.67,
      "text": "With your reflux I'd rather you stop the ibuprofen. I'm going to start you on paracetamol, 1 gram up to four times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 469.6,
      "end_seconds": 477.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.58,
      "text": "I'd also like to start diclofenac gel, rubbed into the wrist three times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 478.06,
      "end_seconds": 489.39,
      "duration_seconds": 11.33,
      "text": "Perfect. Before you start on exercises, soak the hand in warm water, then do gentle wrist circles, ten of them, several times a day. Don't force it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 491.21,
      "end_seconds": 493.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Should I keep drawing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 495.23,
      "end_seconds": 501.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.89,
      "text": "In short stretches, yes, with a break every half hour. No marathon sessions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 503.25,
      "end_seconds": 511.17,
      "duration_seconds": 7.92,
      "text": "Now, come and see me in two weeks, once the X-ray and bloods are back, and bring the diary."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 512.66,
      "end_seconds": 517.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Ha. I'll go and sort the X-ray, then. Thanks, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 519.05,
      "end_seconds": 524.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "No worries at all. Say hello to the mug for me."
    }
  ]
}
